{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>For there is hope</b> — that he may live long when you discipline him." "<b>But do not cause him to die</b> — that he would kill others." "<b>Do not lift up your soul</b> — to sustain him from his plunder, as in the matter of \"and to it he lifts up his soul to sustain himself from it.\"" "Another interpretation: <b>But do not cause him to die</b> — others would kill him; then do not lift up your soul when you discipline him." "Another interpretation: <b>But do not cause him to die</b> — others; if you do not discipline him you will cause him to die, and there will go out from him a great wrath." "Another interpretation: <b>Do not lift up your soul</b> — from him, that you would withhold discipline from him. But the son who is of great wrath — on account of his great wrath, leave him and let him receive his punishment. Like: he bears his iniquity, and do not involve yourself in saving him. For if you save him once, you still need to save him again many times."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:42.800257751Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}